      "response": {
        "text": "Diagnosis:\n- The pricing API latency (p99) has increased to 2600ms, and CPU usage is at 96%.\n- The number of replicas for pricing-api was 3, but logs indicate flash sale traffic (2x normal) and a runbook recommendation to use 6 replicas during sales.\n- The price-cache hit ratio is 0% for the past hour, and logs show the cache is stuck in a loading state after a failed snapshot restore, causing 100% cache misses and forcing the API to compute prices from the catalog.\n\nRemediation steps taken:\n1. Scaled the pricing-api service from 3 to 6 replicas to handle increased load.\n2. Restarted the price-cache service to recover it from the stuck state and restore cache functionality.\n3. Posted a public status update informing customers of the elevated latency and ongoing remediation.\n\nNext steps: Monitor the impact of these actions on latency, CPU, and cache hit ratio.",
